# Topic 2 · Feminist Theories and Practice

::: glance | Topic 2 at a glance
**Head III** of the syllabus. The lightest topic in the descriptive paper — ==7 visits== (six full questions and two short notes, 2016–2025) — but the second-richest source of MCQs (**26 of 140**). Every syllabus school except men's feminism has been asked: radical (2016, 2024), Marxist/socialist (2016, 2021), psychoanalytic (2021), postmodern (2019) and "any two schools" (2022); the applied question "which feminism suits Pakistan?" came in 2018. Since 2024 the examiner has moved beyond the syllabus: intersectionality (2025), and MCQs on standpoint theory, strategic essentialism, kyriarchy, the matrix of domination and the patriarchal bargain (2026). Liberal and men's feminism are due.
:::

